# mossy_rock.fmat — the second-texture blend, as a material.
#
# This was `blend_texture:` and `blend_mask:` on a brush face: two texture names
# to fill in per face, and a mask whose meaning had to be remembered. Naming the
# pair once is the difference between a cliff of forty faces that agree and one
# that nearly does.
#
# The mask is read for LUMINANCE only, so any texture serves: black is the base
# texture, white is the blend one. `dirt` is standing in for a painted mask here
# — swap it for one of your own.
kind: surface
texture: rock
doc: Rock with moss in its hollows. Swap `mask` for a painted one.
effects:
  - effect: blend
    texture: moss
    mask: dirt
  - effect: normal_map
  - effect: smooth
